{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-2_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To address your acid reflux and work towards a healthier and more active lifestyle, consider the following practical steps:\n\n1. Adjust Your Meal Timing: Since you often eat dinner late, try to have your last meal at least two to three hours before bedtime. This helps prevent acid from refluxing when you lie down.\n\n2. Eat Out Less Frequently: Restaurant meals are often richer and larger, which can trigger reflux and contribute to weight gain. When you do eat out, choose lighter, less fatty options, eat slowly, and control your portions.\n\n3. Resume Physical Activity: Start with moderate activities such as daily walks or gentle home workouts. Regular exercise not only helps manage your weight but also reduces acid reflux symptoms.\n\n4. Make Dietary Changes: Focus on a diet rich in fiber, vegetables, fruits, and low-fat foods. Avoid trigger foods like fatty, spicy, or acidic dishes, and limit sugary drinks, alcohol, and caffeine.\n\n5. Lifestyle Modifications: Elevate your head while sleeping, wear loose clothing, and avoid lying down right after eating.\n\n6. Manage Stress: Continue to practice relaxation techniques and ensure you get enough quality sleep.\n\nIf symptoms persist, consult your healthcare provider for further advice or treatment options.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0032-91-00840:11": 32.60469436645508, "clueweb22-en0004-78-00837:7": 32.54142379760742, "clueweb22-en0027-58-19039:6": 32.438072204589844, "clueweb22-en0003-24-03853:5": 31.67980194091797, "clueweb22-en0006-16-16635:6": 31.396970748901367, "clueweb22-en0027-58-19039:9": 30.9949893951416, "clueweb22-en0030-46-19403:8": 30.93459129333496, "clueweb22-en0004-78-00837:8": 30.817859649658203, "clueweb22-en0005-41-09262:20": 30.6973819732666, "clueweb22-en0035-62-03918:7": 30.621673583984375}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I eat dinner late at night.", "I