{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It is not recommended to tape healthy fingers as a preventative measure when training. Research and expert opinion indicate that preventative taping of uninjured fingers is ineffective and could even be potentially harmful. Taping should be reserved for fingers with existing injuries, such as pulley strains or tears, as proper taping (like H-taping) helps support the injured pulley by keeping the tendons close to the bone and preventing further damage.\n\nFor your situation, focus on taping only the injured finger using the H-taping method when you resume climbing. This will provide the necessary support and protection for the healing pulley. Continue to avoid tweaky crimps and maintain good warm-up routines, as these are effective ways to prevent further injuries. Always prioritize proper technique and gradual return to full activity rather than relying on taping as a preventive tool.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 37.210655212402344, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:7": 36.77739334106445, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 36.46544647216797, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:1": 35.39611053466797, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:8": 34.837284088134766, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:3": 34.01799774169922, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 33.838348388671875, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 33.70644760131836, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 33.563697814941406, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 33.46550750732422}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 37.210655212402344, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:7": 36.77739334106445, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 36.46544647216797, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:1": 35.39611053466797, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:8": 34.837284088134766, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:3": 34.01799774169922, "clueweb22-en003