{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "With four months until your 10K run, you have ample time to prepare and build your fitness gradually and safely, which is ideal given your current confidence level.\n\nA typical progression could look like this:\n\n**Weeks 1\u20134 (Base Building):**\n- Run 3 times per week, starting with comfortable runs of 4\u20136 km each.\n- Include one longer run each week, gradually increasing from 6 km to 8 km.\n- Add cross-training (like swimming or cycling) once a week to aid recovery and prevent injury.\n- Incorporate hill workouts or gentle intervals to build strength.\n\n**Weeks 5\u20138 (Mileage Increase):**\n- Increase running to 4 times per week, with total weekly mileage reaching 15\u201320 km.\n- Long runs should reach 9\u201310 km by the end of this phase.\n- Continue cross-training and include some tempo or interval sessions at a controlled pace.\n\n**Weeks 9\u201312 (Race Preparation):**\n- Maintain 4 runs per week, with occasional rest or easy weeks to avoid overtraining.\n- Your long run should be at or slightly above 10 km.\n- Practice race pace during some intervals.\n- Taper your training in the final two weeks, reducing both volume and intensity.\n\nAllow for flexibility and listen to your body. Rest is as important as training, especially for injury prevention and confidence building.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0041-25-14342:3": 33.58671188354492, "clueweb22-en0004-89-17215:4": 33.32448959350586, "clueweb22-en0036-22-19114:2": 33.28151321411133, "clueweb22-en0014-59-09526:11": 33.06263732910156, "clueweb22-en0031-62-14539:5": 32.976173400878906, "clueweb22-en0026-77-06464:5": 32.57746505737305, "clueweb22-en0014-95-05002:12": 32.5046501159668, "clueweb22-en0000-55-01473:1": 32.41425323486328, "clueweb22-en0004-20-06628:10": 32.330474853515625, "clueweb22-en0033-03-08847:4": 32.32460403442383}, "ptkb_provenan