{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It is wonderful to hear that you are feeling confident and prepared for motherhood. While every baby is unique, it is important to remember that some crying is natural and normal for all infants. Crying is how babies communicate\u2014they might be hungry, tired, uncomfortable, or simply need to be close to you. Breastfeeding provides not only essential nutrition but also comfort and emotional closeness, which can help soothe your baby and reduce crying episodes.\n\nIf your baby does cry, it does not mean you are doing anything wrong; it is simply their way of expressing needs. Responding with affection and care, offering feeds, cuddles, and attention, will help your baby feel secure and loved. Over time, you will learn to recognize your baby\u2019s different cries and what they need.\n\nYou are already showing great care and commitment, which is the most important thing for your child\u2019s wellbeing. Trust yourself and reach out for support if you need it\u2014you are not alone on this journey.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0006-02-13781:3": 24.677139282226562, "clueweb22-en0005-46-00778:1": 24.483562469482422, "clueweb22-en0012-14-02860:1": 24.38035774230957, "clueweb22-en0045-42-02950:10": 23.94010353088379, "clueweb22-en0034-27-16750:0": 23.819704055786133, "clueweb22-en0037-81-01263:5": 23.782569885253906, "clueweb22-en0014-95-00318:11": 23.44567108154297, "clueweb22-en0005-46-00778:0": 23.43851089477539, "clueweb22-en0028-20-07787:8": 23.381057739257812, "clueweb22-en0012-14-02860:2": 23.34292984008789}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0006-02-13781:3": 24.677139282226562, "clueweb22-en0005-46-00778:1": 24.483562469482422, "clueweb22-en0012-14-02860:1": 24.38035774230957, "clueweb22-en0045-42-02950:10": 23.94010353088379, "clueweb22-en0034-27-16750:0": 23.819704055786133, "clue