{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The main difference between fractional CO2 laser treatments and fully ablative CO2 lasers lies in intensity, recovery time, and risk.\n\nFully ablative CO2 lasers remove the entire surface layer of the targeted skin area. This leads to dramatic results, particularly for deep wrinkles or significant sun damage, but comes with significant downtime, greater discomfort, and higher risk of side effects. It is most suitable for lighter skin tones, and recovery can take up to two weeks or more.\n\nFractional CO2 lasers, on the other hand, use a pixelated pattern to treat only a fraction of the skin at a time. Small zones are targeted, leaving surrounding skin intact, which speeds up healing and reduces risk. Fractional treatments are less aggressive, require minimal downtime, and are customizable to your needs. However, they usually require multiple sessions for optimal results.\n\nGiven your preference for minimal downtime, fractional CO2 laser resurfacing would be the most appropriate of the two, offering noticeable improvement with less recovery.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:9": 26.158166885375977, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:10": 26.025768280029297, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:12": 24.548948287963867, "clueweb22-en0031-16-03068:4": 24.524864196777344, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:11": 24.060142517089844, "clueweb22-en0025-73-01656:9": 23.507158279418945, "clueweb22-en0046-40-14664:2": 23.48999786376953, "clueweb22-en0039-50-11586:13": 23.11522102355957, "clueweb22-en0025-73-01656:10": 22.949228286743164, "clueweb22-en0032-95-20516:4": 22.622987747192383}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with minimal downtime."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:9": 26.158166885375977, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:10": 26.025768280029297, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:12": 24.5489482879