{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After microneedling, it is important to avoid using products that contain strong exfoliating acids, such as salicylic acid (BHA), for at least 24\u201348 hours post-treatment. This is because freshly treated skin is more sensitive and susceptible to irritation, and salicylic acid could increase redness or discomfort.\n\nFor your oily skin and scalp, you should continue your usual hair care routine, as microneedling does not affect the scalp unless the procedure is performed there. However, for your facial routine, temporarily discontinue your salicylic acid face wash immediately after microneedling. Instead, use a gentle, non-irritating cleanser during the initial recovery period.\n\nOnce 48 hours have passed and your skin has calmed, you may gradually reintroduce salicylic acid into your regimen, monitoring your skin\u2019s response. During the first two days, prioritize hydration by applying hyaluronic acid and protecting your skin with sunscreen. Avoid retinol, AHA, BHA, and vitamin C serums immediately post-procedure to minimize the risk of irritation.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0000-17-14795:15": 36.3037109375, "clueweb22-en0033-91-06135:10": 35.37725830078125, "clueweb22-en0000-24-11991:12": 34.55633544921875, "clueweb22-en0032-74-03879:8": 34.3722038269043, "clueweb22-en0038-01-18087:7": 34.36125183105469, "clueweb22-en0005-72-07792:4": 33.893306732177734, "clueweb22-en0042-13-06743:10": 33.712520599365234, "clueweb22-en0027-79-08527:13": 33.39189529418945, "clueweb22-en0007-64-08658:11": 33.28306579589844, "clueweb22-en0011-29-01443:15": 32.99189376831055}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I use vitamin C and Retinol every day in my morning routine.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I use AHA BHA serum once a week.", "I apply Hyaluronic Acid two times a day after washing my face."]}], "references": {"clue