{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Shampoos containing niacinamide and lactic acid or LHA can indeed be beneficial for oily scalps, as these ingredients help balance sebum production, gently exfoliate the scalp, and promote a healthier scalp environment. In addition to choosing the right shampoo, consider the following tips for managing oily hair:\n\n- Wash your hair frequently, ideally at least four times per week, using a deep-cleansing or balancing shampoo.\n- Avoid moisturizing or hydrating shampoos and conditioners, as they can increase oiliness.\n- Apply conditioner only to the ends of your hair, not the scalp, to prevent excess oil buildup.\n- Incorporate a clarifying shampoo occasionally to remove buildup from styling products and natural oils, but avoid overuse to prevent scalp irritation.\n- Use a dry shampoo between washes for quick oil absorption.\n- Detoxify your scalp with gentle exfoliating scalp masks to remove buildup and maintain scalp health.\n- Change your pillowcase weekly to reduce oil and dirt transfer.\n- Since you frequently use heat styling tools, be mindful to use lightweight, non-oily styling products to avoid further weighing down your hair.\n\nIf scalp irritation persists, consider consulting a dermatologist for tailored advice.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-41-10440:5": 36.700340270996094, "clueweb22-en0008-22-09694:9": 35.43344497680664, "clueweb22-en0042-65-10707:4": 35.39979553222656, "clueweb22-en0018-54-01822:10": 35.02643585205078, "clueweb22-en0009-83-04895:8": 34.820987701416016, "clueweb22-en0037-41-10440:4": 34.54899597167969, "clueweb22-en0020-81-06334:7": 34.47250747680664, "clueweb22-en0044-61-03851:10": 34.44619369506836, "clueweb22-en0020-26-07211:6": 34.43453598022461, "clueweb22-en0043-96-12746:6": 34.353736877441406}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I frequently use heat styling tools to keep my hair looking good