{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Given your interest in healthy options, both lavash and Turkish flatbread are excellent choices. They are traditional breads known for their nutritious ingredients and versatility. Lavash is particularly thin and can be made with just flour, water, and salt, making it low in calories and suitable for wraps or as a side to salads\u2014something that pairs well with your habit of eating raw salads. Turkish flatbread tends to be slightly thicker and uses yeast, resulting in a fluffier texture, which can also be used for sandwiches or as a healthy accompaniment to meals.\n\nIf you want a bread that helps you feel fuller with fewer calories and carbohydrates, wholegrain versions of either bread are ideal. Both can be baked at home using basic baking skills, and lavash, in particular, is simple to make and can be refreshed easily if it becomes leathery. Either option will support your focus on healthy eating while providing variety for your home baking.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0041-64-01489:3": 37.02494812011719, "clueweb22-en0023-44-17198:11": 35.00272750854492, "clueweb22-en0041-64-01489:2": 34.20751953125, "clueweb22-en0003-53-18240:10": 34.1312370300293, "clueweb22-en0044-75-13848:4": 33.96553039550781, "clueweb22-en0023-44-17198:10": 33.54335021972656, "clueweb22-en0026-42-03191:0": 32.96415710449219, "clueweb22-en0003-10-15963:0": 32.74444580078125, "clueweb22-en0044-75-13848:3": 31.96310806274414, "clueweb22-en0024-95-17600:0": 31.89057731628418}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I often eat raw salads.", "I go to the gym twice a week.", "I have some basic baking experience."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0041-64-01489:3": 37.02494812011719, "clueweb22-en0023-44-17198:11": 35.00272750854492, "clueweb22-en0041-64-01489:2": 34.20751953125, "clueweb22-en0003-53-18240:10": 34.1312370300293, "clueweb22-en0044-75-13848:4": 33.965