{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Feeling overwhelmed by a large number of tasks is a common experience for adults with ADHD. To address this, consider breaking large tasks into smaller, manageable steps and prioritizing them. Creating a daily or weekly checklist can help you focus on what truly needs to be done and reduce feelings of overload. Scheduling routine tasks at consistent times each week can also bring structure and predictability.\n\nUsing a task manager for to-dos and a calendar for time-sensitive activities can help you organize your workload and free up mental space. Setting deadlines, even for smaller steps, can give you a sense of progress and control. If you find yourself struggling to start or complete tasks, try using time-management techniques like the Pomodoro Technique\u2014work in short, focused intervals with planned breaks.\n\nLastly, if a particular strategy feels difficult or isn\u2019t working, don\u2019t hesitate to adjust your approach or seek support from colleagues or organized peers. Consistency is key, but it\u2019s also important to find what best suits your needs and preferences.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0001-03-06965:6": 22.33629608154297, "clueweb22-en0039-55-00787:1": 21.868499755859375, "clueweb22-en0002-41-06891:5": 21.100341796875, "clueweb22-en0022-96-02784:6": 20.899168014526367, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 20.861249923706055, "clueweb22-en0040-44-04493:7": 20.84516143798828, "clueweb22-en0022-45-10048:7": 20.813392639160156, "clueweb22-en0041-23-00835:21": 20.23198127746582, "clueweb22-en0042-03-14870:5": 20.169456481933594, "clueweb22-en0023-70-01917:23": 19.591073989868164}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I love it when it is quiet.", "I work in an office."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0001-03-06965:6": 22.33629608154297, "clueweb22-en0039-55-00787:1": 21.868499755859375, "clueweb22-en0002-41-06891:5": 21.