{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Getting started with tattooing involves several important steps:\n\n1. **Develop Your Artistic Skills:** Focus on building a strong portfolio with designs specifically suited for tattoos. Your portfolio should showcase your ability to create clear, bold, and original artwork.\n\n2. **Seek an Apprenticeship:** Approach reputable tattoo shops and artists, spending time in their environment to build relationships. Apprenticeships are highly competitive and typically unpaid, lasting one to three years. Expect to start with basic, often menial tasks while learning from experienced artists.\n\n3. **Practice Fundamentals:** Before working on real skin, practice tattooing on fake skin, such as pigskin, to develop skills in outlining, shading, coloring, and lettering. Observe your mentor\u2019s techniques closely to improve.\n\n4. **Meet Legal and Health Requirements:** After your apprenticeship, register with your local council for a license and fulfill any necessary health requirements, such as hepatitis B vaccination.\n\n5. **Persistence and Dedication:** The journey requires patience, hard work, and dedication. Building a client base takes time, and income often depends on the number of clients you tattoo.\n\nChoosing the right mentor is crucial for learning both the art and business aspects of tattooing, ensuring you develop into a skilled and responsible artist.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0016-15-15694:2": 25.809598922729492, "clueweb22-en0016-15-15694:3": 24.846010208129883, "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:14": 24.315465927124023, "clueweb22-en0015-05-03360:11": 24.185428619384766, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:8": 23.91098403930664, "clueweb22-en0028-52-08765:2": 23.75850486755371, "clueweb22-en0028-52-08765:1": 23.64514923095703, "clueweb22-en0031-91-19741:4": 23.6035213470459, "clueweb22-en0018-35-02125:19": 23.4939479827880