{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly! Tattoo needles come in various types, each suited for different techniques:\n\n1. **Round Liners (RL):** Used for outlining. The needles are grouped in a circle\u2014great for crisp lines.\n2. **Round Shaders (RS):** Arranged similarly to liners but with a bit of space between the needles. Ideal for shading small areas and adding detail.\n3. **Magnums (M1/M2):** These are flat and wide, making them perfect for shading and coloring larger areas. M1 is stacked (needles in two rows); M2 is double stacked for more coverage.\n4. **Flat Needles (F):** Needles lined up in a straight row, often used for geometric shapes and shading.\n\nFor starting out, having a selection of round liners (for outlines) and magnums (for shading/color) will cover most basic designs. Always use sterile, single-use needles to maintain strict hygiene.\n\nWould you like tips on how to choose the right size or how to handle them safely?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0029-38-05666:18": 22.06399917602539, "clueweb22-en0033-74-18753:1": 21.70132827758789, "clueweb22-en0007-89-03397:1": 21.70132827758789, "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:8": 21.567214965820312, "clueweb22-en0024-22-17473:7": 21.1719913482666, "clueweb22-en0038-43-13061:12": 21.125259399414062, "clueweb22-en0045-52-15422:2": 21.008087158203125, "clueweb22-en0044-23-02538:13": 20.801523208618164, "clueweb22-en0033-74-18753:0": 20.775249481201172, "clueweb22-en0007-89-03397:0": 20.775249481201172}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I can draw well."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0029-38-05666:18": 22.06399917602539, "clueweb22-en0033-74-18753:1": 21.70132827758789, "clueweb22-en0007-89-03397:1": 21.70132827758789, "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:8": 21.567214965820312, "clueweb22-en0024-22-17473:7": 21.1719913482666, "clueweb22-en0038-43-13061:12": 21.125259399414062, "clueweb22-en0045-52-15422:2": 21.0