{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "When choosing new pedals for your mountain bike, especially given your preference for comfort and riding in varied, sometimes wet, conditions, focus on the following key features:\n\n1. Material: Opt for pedals made from durable metals like aluminum, which offer better longevity and grip than plastic, especially on rough or muddy trails.\n2. Platform Size: A wider platform offers greater stability and distributes pressure more evenly, which is beneficial for comfort during longer rides and helps if you experience back pain.\n3. Traction Pins: Look for pedals with metal traction pins; they prevent your feet from slipping, even in wet or muddy conditions.\n4. Bearings: Sealed bearings are preferable\u2014they keep out dirt and moisture, ensuring smooth rotation and reducing maintenance.\n5. Weather Resistance: Since you ride in rainy weather, choose pedals with a slip-resistant surface and corrosion-resistant materials.\n6. Weight: While lighter pedals can be appealing, prioritize comfort and grip over minimal weight, as speed is not your main concern.\n7. Sustainability: If possible, select pedals that are repairable or made from recycled materials to align with your sustainability values.\n\nThese features will provide you with comfort, control, and safety across forest paths and hilly city terrain.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0025-89-12241:4": 27.250972747802734, "clueweb22-en0005-77-14165:1": 26.926197052001953, "clueweb22-en0004-58-12409:15": 26.793153762817383, "clueweb22-en0006-31-17607:3": 26.716943740844727, "clueweb22-en0020-92-06373:1": 26.482921600341797, "clueweb22-en0031-11-03184:9": 26.369667053222656, "clueweb22-en0043-36-07774:3": 26.352087020874023, "clueweb22-en0032-20-03792:6": 26.311288833618164, "clueweb22-en0013-40-05916:14": 26.260543823242188, "clueweb22-en0040-31-08734:4": 26.257579803466797}, 