{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Given your focus on comfort, casual riding style, and preference for flexibility, clipless pedals may not be the best fit for your needs. Clipless pedals are designed to maximize pedaling efficiency and are favored by riders focused on training or competitive cycling; they require special cycling shoes and a learning period to get used to clipping in and out, which can feel less intuitive, especially on uneven or hilly terrain.\n\nFlat pedals, by contrast, are beginner-friendly, safer to use when riding in forests or in wet conditions, and allow you to wear any shoe with good tread. They offer flexibility for quick stops and maneuvering, which is beneficial on rough or unpredictable paths. Many modern flat pedals provide excellent grip and stability, addressing most comfort and control concerns for casual riders.\n\nIf you want the option to use both regular and cycling shoes, dual-platform pedals (flat on one side, clipless on the other) exist, but for your comfort-focused, casual riding, high-quality flat pedals are usually the most practical and enjoyable choice.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-57-01381:4": 33.059818267822266, "clueweb22-en0021-36-08429:13": 30.76461410522461, "clueweb22-en0037-60-07465:5": 30.527141571044922, "clueweb22-en0026-14-04520:10": 30.162113189697266, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:5": 30.071674346923828, "clueweb22-en0034-51-14697:0": 30.052982330322266, "clueweb22-en0021-36-08429:12": 29.98695182800293, "clueweb22-en0023-47-11728:6": 29.712461471557617, "clueweb22-en0001-22-06023:3": 29.694055557250977, "clueweb22-en0000-09-06499:10": 29.587739944458008}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I value comfort over speed.", "I'm a casual bike rider.", "I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest.", "I sometimes get overwhelmed by too ma