{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_true-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You should lubricate your bike chain and drivetrain components when you notice the chain becoming dry, noisy, or after riding in wet, muddy, or rainy conditions, which wash away lubricant more quickly. If you ride frequently in the forest or in the rain, it\u2019s recommended to check your chain regularly. \n\nA well-lubricated chain runs smoothly and quietly. If you begin to hear squeaking, clicking, or grinding noises, or if the chain feels rough when pedaling, it is a sign that lubrication is needed. You can also visually inspect the chain\u2014if it looks dry or has visible rust, dirt, or debris, it\u2019s time for cleaning and lubrication.\n\nAfter thoroughly cleaning the chain with a rag and degreaser, dry it completely before applying new lubricant. Always wipe off any excess to avoid attracting dirt. Regular maintenance will help prevent unnecessary wear and ensure your bike performs well in all conditions.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0020-44-10600:11": 27.007461547851562, "clueweb22-en0022-60-04492:3": 26.93007469177246, "clueweb22-en0013-24-07348:6": 26.898605346679688, "clueweb22-en0021-76-15035:8": 26.642744064331055, "clueweb22-en0000-80-11057:10": 26.611474990844727, "clueweb22-en0007-13-11098:6": 26.451648712158203, "clueweb22-en0043-38-08959:4": 26.37824249267578, "clueweb22-en0022-60-04492:4": 26.205900192260742, "clueweb22-en0001-88-16406:5": 25.76106834411621, "clueweb22-en0000-80-11057:11": 25.6444034576416}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0020-44-10600:11": 27.007461547851562, "clueweb22-en0022-60-04492:3": 26.93007469177246, "clueweb22-en0013-24-07348:6": 26.898605346679688, "clueweb22-en0021-76-15035:8": 26.642744064331055, "clueweb22-en0000-80-11057:10": 26.611474990844727, "clueweb22-en0007-13-11098:6": 26.4516487121